  "title": "The NLA reads position from the part of the vector Oracle Lens's words do not rebuild",
  "caption": "Exp 16, layer 42, 200 items per row. Each activation is split into the part the NLA's reconstructor rebuilds from Oracle Lens's bullets (the Oracle Lens part) and the remainder (what those words do not rebuild); one part is swapped in from a donor item of the opposite class. Dots: AUROC of the NLA's prompted log-odds (mean of 4 phrasings) against the donor's label; bands: 95% bootstrap CI clustered by passage (2,000 resamples). Position rows follow the remainder; the language control follows the Oracle Lens part. Caveat: both parts are built with the NLA's reconstructor; one seeded donor pairing.",
